  nonce: '1783'  # 1783
  message: "DONE in PR #2038 (dev d360ff18d8; lab /home/jgstern_agent/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/sosov_11032026/RESULT.md, pre-registered in PREREGISTER.md). Two commits. (1) A function's parameters are reaching definitions at its own line: cfg.solve_reaching_defs(cfg, entry_defs) numbers them as entry-block definitions (no CFG statement, so stmt_defuse / unaccounted_names / the coverage gate are untouched), LanguageDdgSpec.params_for for python / js-ts / go, RepoDdg.params; verdict-inert as pre-registered: verify-claims on the Express and Flask probes and the curriculum express and caddy repos, 28 of 28 claims identical. (2) The seed: taint.parameter_seeds mints a ParameterSeed(handler, parameter, line, source, represents) per request_ingress entry with a contract (REQUEST_PARAMETER_CONTRACTS: express_route arg 0, go_handler the *http.Request-typed parameter; GENERIC_ROUTE_CONTRACTS for the generic http_route the analyzers actually file Express and Go HandleFunc handlers under, by language: js/ts arg 0, go typed, python none) whose handler the DDG walked and whose parameter has a use from its entry definition (no use, no seed: the handler stays clean AND listed); a route MARKER entry (Go HandleFunc) seeds what it dispatches_to and represents the marker. propagate_taint_ddg(parameter_seeds=) walks it as a pseudo-callee entry from the handler's line with the parameter as the seeded variable (never one call with the sink; a sink on the parameter's own line counts: the one-line arrow); the structural arm takes NO parameter seed (the item's warning). represented_ingress_callers(parameter_seeds=) narrows the TAINT arm's disclosure; the BOUNDARY arm keeps naming the handler (_verify(unseeded_ingress_boundary=), 'no net_recv crossing represents'): no crossing stands behind a parameter, so a webserver cannot confirm 'never receives network data' because its request was followed (ADR-0049 ruling 3). BEHAVIOURAL EVIDENCE (production-path tests, core/tests/test_request_parameter_seed.py + the updated test_verify_claims_unseeded_ingress.py): the Express probe's untrusted-input-no-host-fs goes inconclusive -> VIOLATED, precise, through req -> fs.writeFileSync for both the multi-line and the one-line handler, /save /echo /one leave the taint disclosure, /ping (never reads req) stays listed with no flow; the Go ServeHTTP and HandleFunc probes the same through r -> os.WriteFile; never-receives-network-data stays withheld naming every handler. Corpus A/B (fuzik generic claims, base worktree at dev ceca2f496c): Express probe host-fs inconclusive -> violated (precise) and the handler leaves the untrusted_input disclosures; Flask probe 7/7 identical; curriculum express 7/7 identical (its ingress entries are example/test markers; probing the hop there found the cross-file dispatch and the error-middleware shapes, both guarded before commit); caddy 7/7 identical with its 28 ServeHTTP handlers represented (5 read against source). Six mutations each red on exactly their own tests (no-use requirement, typed match, represented union, same-line allowance, same-file hop guard, error-middleware arity rule). Pre-registered and NOT done: Django views (request is arg 0 of a django_view: a contract row away, unmeasured), JS meta.params (not needed: RepoDdg.params carries the names), user-vouched contracts (the shipped table is builtin)."  # 1783
